# Deterministic checkouts across Windows, macOS, and Linux.
#
# TailTrail verifies byte hashes in several places (official-pack manifests,
# adapter integrity, revision stamps). A CRLF checkout of an LF-pinned file
# changes every hash, so verification would pass on one OS and fail on
# another. These rules override per-machine core.autocrlf and keep worktree
# bytes identical everywhere.
* text=auto
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.mdc text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.csv text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.svg text eol=lf
*.diff text eol=lf
*.log text eol=lf
*.in text eol=lf
*.gitignore text eol=lf
*.png binary
*.whl binary
*.zip binary
*.tar.gz binary
